Biotopes: grows in sandy soil, under hardwood (Fagus), (Betula), (Quercus);
Pileus 8-15 mm Ã˜, Â± conical at first, convex to spreading, slightly depressed, Â± nippled, fibrillated and squamous, Â± mechuleux towards the center, Â± spiky, brown to reddish brown, darker in the center;
Gills indented to sinuate, spaced to sub-spaced, with lamellae and lamellules, broad to subventrous, yellowish cream, with whitish border;
Stipe 13-19 Ã— 1-2 mm Ã˜, cylindrical, full, with small whitish fibrils at the apex, sub-bulbose, reddish-brown, curving slightly at the base;
